#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133899 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133715 :question/id #uuid "18eef985-0fd4-5b08-8072-684ded227ab4" :question/math-academy-id "e-9557" :question/problem "![](images/16/16026d4ac7deeb30c1abb3a066df23a06a544116463b364b0a1e9e0bac0608c8.png)\n\nSuppose that $\\mathbf F$ is a vector field on $\\mathbb R^2$ defined over the region $D$ above. Given that \n\n$$\n\\oint\\limits_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\textrm d \\mathbf r = 10, \n\\qquad \n\\oint\\limits_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\textrm d \\mathbf r = -8, \n\\qquad \n\\oint\\limits_{C_3}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\textrm d \\mathbf r = 3,\n$$\n\nwhere $C_1$ and $C_3$ are oriented clockwise, and $C_2$ is oriented counterclockwise, calculate the value of $\\displaystyle\\oint\\limits_{\\partial D}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\textrm d \\mathbf r.$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the total circulation of a vector field over the boundary of a region containing holes, we add together the circulations over each *positively oriented* boundary.\n\nRemember that:\n\n- the positive direction is *counterclockwise* for the *outer* curve $C_1$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse $C_1$ counterclockwise), and\n\n- the positive direction is *clockwise* for the *inner* curves $C_2$ and $C_3$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse $C_2$ and $C_3$ clockwise).\n\nThe diagram below shows the positive orientations of all three curves.\n\n![](images/11/11445c083440ee2fde1864d599a8bbd68146d522c61de11b3e90dc231e6eddf1.png)\n\nNotice that the positive orientations of the outer curve $C_1$ and the inner curve $C_2$ are opposite those stated in the question.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & =-{∮}_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{∮}_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{∮}_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =-10-(-8)+3 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "56caab23-f54d-58ee-99db-99c651f78e5c" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050773 :topic/math-academy-id 3713 :topic/title "Circulation"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134098 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a29028a4-0f8a-5b2f-99f1-47815863bc92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2π" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130745} {:answer/id #uuid "cc41a40b-917a-57ad-93c5-f9db0205c2ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130746} {:answer/id #uuid "34e14694-9434-5ad9-aa2d-2969b9ae1cc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130747} {:answer/id #uuid "4b2ce2f4-0374-5148-947b-96f3d8b6b4ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130748} {:answer/id #uuid "5d7d99a7-294b-5cf9-90af-ed4075071bb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130749}] :answer-field/id #uuid "59065be7-12d4-5585-856f-70e63556d4de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130744}] :question/id #uuid "aa43bdf8-83a8-50c7-a713-6a675dec7cf1" :question/math-academy-id "q-126558" :question/problem "![](images/72/7264984a1c19c247c030feae04615bb0c46205ca70475db1240db964ad6007b2.png)\n\nSuppose that $F$ is a vector field on $R^{2}$ defined over the region $D$ above. Given that\n\n$∮_(C_{1})F \\cdot dr = 10, ∮_(C_{2})F \\cdot dr =-4, ∮_(C_{3})F \\cdot dr =-2$,\n\nwhere $C_{1}$ is oriented counterclockwise and $C_{2}$ and $C_{3}$ are oriented clockwise, calculate the value of $∮_(∂D)F \\cdot dr$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134102 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f8dac37b-0c3a-5985-b30b-b455cf17748a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130769} {:answer/id #uuid "0f82c5b5-9ec9-5493-9c5e-088d8f3b2063" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130770} {:answer/id #uuid "226dc38b-e879-5d2e-a506-237fa0f69c69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130771} {:answer/id #uuid "6b90ef5b-f492-5c0a-b77c-3339c17e5782" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130772} {:answer/id #uuid "6c604190-84cc-5e3c-a8c7-3b023549d9b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130773}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "226dc38b-e879-5d2e-a506-237fa0f69c69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130771} :answer-field/id #uuid "031169e4-3e81-5b19-b1f4-b5af34d5e90a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130768}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d0e6048a-c528-5a8c-b47d-ee8959e52035" :question/math-academy-id "q-126654" :question/problem "![](images/cb/cbe865077b446bdd97c290cef0924d3f17807a9e1039c9be45f4aa6e4b29cc3c.png)\n\nSuppose that $F$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ defined over the region $D$ above. Given that \n\n$$\n{∮}_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=1,\\,{∮}_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=5,\\,{∮}_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=-3,\n$$\n\nwhere ${C}_{1},$ ${C}_{2},$ and ${C}_{3}$ are oriented counterclockwise, calculate the value of ${∮}_{∂D}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the total circulation of a vector field over the boundary of a region containing holes, we add together the circulations over each *positively oriented* boundary.\n\nRemember that:\n\n- the positive direction is *counterclockwise* for the *outer* curve ${C}_{1}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{1}$ counterclockwise), and\n\n- the positive direction is *clockwise* for the *inner* curves ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ clockwise).\n\nThe diagram below shows the positive orientations of all three curves.\n\n![](images/fd/fd221ae68fc4983fb0a3f7a745154764e5c0081b2b9b66e7f8ad4a150a8b3bc5.png)\n\nNotice that the positive orientations of the inner curves ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ are opposite to those stated in the question.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={∮}_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{∮}_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{∮}_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =1-5-(-3) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369462 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d7cf9a0-e8a9-528c-9faf-b2259025de3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369464} {:answer/id #uuid "ce1af42a-4bf9-5730-a278-44c2bcb271c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369465} {:answer/id #uuid "26f52db4-19ad-52bc-bdea-a43ddccabe76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369466} {:answer/id #uuid "74b55cd4-e132-5c25-af68-783e5644f0be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369467} {:answer/id #uuid "5901a191-1792-51d7-92cf-8ae7fe658d89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369468}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5901a191-1792-51d7-92cf-8ae7fe658d89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369468} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0c368b0-4e71-50a8-b81a-cf6d68ab083b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369463}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ca63e980-b1ab-5e66-b1ce-ccb3144f7558" :question/math-academy-id "q-126862" :question/problem "![](images/49/49b14da54c952d0585f7aa894d618838ddc91beb65216e0c18c014ba5ad268d7.png)\n\nSuppose that $F$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ defined over the region $D$ above. Given that \n\n$$\n{∮}_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=9,\\,{∮}_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=-4,\\,{∮}_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=-6,\n$$\n\nwhere ${C}_{1}$ is oriented counterclockwise and ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ are oriented clockwise, calculate the value of ${∮}_{∂D}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the total circulation of a vector field over the boundary of a region containing holes, we add together the circulations over each *positively oriented* boundary.\n\nRemember that:\n\n- the positive direction is *counterclockwise* for the *outer* curve ${C}_{1}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{1}$ counterclockwise), and\n\n- the positive direction is *clockwise* for the *inner* curves ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ clockwise).\n\nThe diagram below shows the positive orientations of all three curves.\n\n![](images/a8/a8e93055fb9a460ab7757475c9c381c191204eae72231921da870b8d727bf988.png)\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={∮}_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{∮}_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{∮}_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =9+(-4)+(-6) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369469 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c0b304ac-2b36-5437-b9d8-5fcf23fa4d1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369471} {:answer/id #uuid "a879fd91-6ea0-5ab3-ad43-e4706f2d1bc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369472} {:answer/id #uuid "b0f30d72-4cc9-59bd-b370-c87bbec40944" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369473} {:answer/id #uuid "a8834855-579a-54da-8ae2-aa6847585195" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4"